## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to reason about regional isolation, backpressure propagation, and observability. Probes engineering judgment for multi-region reliability, fault tolerance, and rollback safety. Requires practical implementation patterns including token buckets, DLQs, 429 signaling, and synthetic testing.

## Key Concepts
- Region-scoped capacity and quotas
- Backpressure signaling and circuit breaking
- DLQ and retry semantics
- Observability fusion (metrics, traces, logs)
- Testing strategies: canary deployments, synthetic traffic, chaos injection
- Rollback criteria and safety gates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo token bucket limiter for regional ingress
class RegionalTokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, capacity) {
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.rate = rate;
    this.lastRefill = Date.now();
  }

  tryConsume(tokens) {
    this.refill();
    if (this.tokens >= tokens) {
      this.tokens -= tokens;
      return { allowed: true, remaining: this.tokens };
    }
    return {
      allowed: false,
      remaining: this.tokens,
      retryAfter: Math.ceil((tokens - this.tokens) / this.rate)
    };
  }

  refill() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.lastRefill) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.rate);
    this.lastRefill = now;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to diagnose rate-limiter issues, design clear observability, and execute a controlled rollback with minimal disruption.

## Key Concepts
- Token bucket rate limiting across regions
- Observability for distributed systems
- Canary testing and safe traffic shifts
- Rollback and validation under time pressure
- Post-incident analysis and preventive fixes

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo token bucket core (simplified)
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, capacity) { this.rate = rate; this.capacity = capacity; this.tokens = capacity; this.last = Date.now(); }
  allow() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const delta = (now - this.last) * this.rate / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + delta);
    this.last = now;
    if (this.tokens >= 1) { this.tokens -= 1; return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```

